---
source: forge/src/init/render.rs
expression: "format!(\"{}\\n{}\\n{}\", render_host(HOST, &answers, SIGNER),\nrender_person(PERSON, &answers), point_readme(README, \"rec\", \"in\"))"
---
# One machine, one file: `nix run .#init` writes your own host from this file.
{
  configurations.nixos."rec" = {
    system = "x86_64-linux";

    profile = "laptop";

    features = [
      "disk" # LUKS and btrfs, `/` wiped at every boot
      # "secure-boot" # lanzaboote with its own keys
      # "fido2" # a security key logs in and runs sudo
      # "wipe-home" # an empty /home at every boot, needs disk
      # "plymouth" # graphical boot splash
      # "greetd" # the tuigreet login screen
      "docker" # rootless Docker
      # "libvirt" # virtual machines with virt-manager
      # "nix-ld" # run binaries not built for NixOS
      # "ssh" # key-only SSH server
      # "printing" # CUPS with driverless network printers
      # "auto-upgrade" # daily, the version CI validated
    ];

    hardware = [
      # "common-pc-ssd" # nixos-hardware: weekly TRIM
      # "firmware" # redistributable firmware
      # "audio" # PipeWire
      # "bluetooth" # Bluetooth, powered on at boot
      "nvidia" # NVIDIA GPU with the open kernel module
      # "raspberry-pi-5" # Raspberry Pi 5, aarch64-linux
      "framework-13-7040-amd"
    ];

    apps = [
      # "hyprland" # Hyprland through uwsm
      # "waybar" # a top bar
      # "fuzzel" # an app launcher
      # "kitty" # a terminal
      # "mako" # a notification daemon
      # "lock" # a lock screen
      # "upgrade-notify" # a notification after an auto-upgrade
      # "direnv" # per-project dev shells
      "firefox" # Firefox with telemetry off
      # "zsh" # zsh with suggestions
      "vlc"
    ];

    flake = "/home/in/nixos";
    # mirrors = [ "https://codeberg.org/in/nixos.git" ]; # other copies of your fork
    signers = [
      "ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIFake deploy"
    ]; # keys signing deploy/<host>; init writes yours

    timeZone = "Europe/Paris"; # such as "UTC"
    locale = "fr_FR.UTF-8"; # such as "en_US.UTF-8"
    keyboard = "fr"; # such as "us"

    users."in" = {
      # admin = false; # true by default: may run sudo
    };
  };
}

# One person, one folder. A host gives them an account with `users."in"`
# (modules/hosts/example), and `nix run .#init` writes your own person from this file.
{
  users."in" = {
    fullName = "Bob \"the\" Builder \${x}";

    email = "bob@example.net";

    # Public SSH keys allowed to log in as in.
    sshKeys = [ ];

    apps = [
      "zsh" # zsh with suggestions
      "git" # git, the person's name and email are the author
    ];

    # Any other file of modules/users/in may set part of it.
    # module = { pkgs, ... }: { home.packages = [ pkgs.gimp ]; };
  };
}

# A fork

Your [`rec`](modules/hosts/rec/default.nix) host lists every profile, feature, hardware module and app upstream shipped when you ran `nix run .#init`, one line each, commented out when you did not pick it. Read it top to bottom and keep what you like.

1. Run `nix run .#init`, which:
   - writes your host, [`modules/hosts/rec/default.nix`](modules/hosts/rec/default.nix), from the example host and your person, [`modules/users/in/default.nix`](modules/users/in/default.nix), from the example person;
   - removes the examples.
